## Instructions

This form must be completed by every senior/key person listed on a federal proposal or active federal award. It follows the format required by the NSF Proposal & Award Policies & Procedures Guide (PAPPG, effective January 2024) and is compatible with the NIH Other Support format. Personnel using SciENcv to generate their disclosure should use this form as the authoritative source of information to enter into SciENcv.

**When to complete this form:**

1. **At proposal submission.** Each senior/key person must submit a completed form as part of the proposal package (see Proposal Routing and Approval Policy, Stage 3).
2. **Annual update.** Each senior/key person on an active federal award must submit an updated form within 30 days of the award anniversary date, or as required by the sponsoring agency, whichever is earlier.
3. **Within 30 days of any new support.** If you receive a new award, enter into a new consulting arrangement, or begin receiving in-kind support from any source after your most recent disclosure, you must submit an updated form within 30 days.

**What to disclose:** All current and pending support from ALL sources --- federal, state, local, foreign, and private --- regardless of whether the support is related to the current proposal. This includes grants, contracts, cooperative agreements, consulting arrangements, in-kind contributions, and any other resource made available to you in support of or related to your research endeavors. There is no materiality threshold; all support must be reported.

**Where to submit:** Completed forms go to the Grant Officer (Board Chair). Retain a copy for your records.

